@bitwarden/sdk-napi (optional dependency, not bundled)
-----------------------------------------------------
The Secrets Manager tools use @bitwarden/sdk-napi and its per-platform
binary packages (@bitwarden/sdk-napi-<platform>). They are an optional
npm dependency: npm installs them from the npm registry next to this
package; neither this repository nor its npm package contains or
redistributes them. They are not licensed under the MIT License of this
project but under the Bitwarden Software Development Kit License
Agreement (the LICENSE file of those packages, "SEE LICENSE IN LICENSE"
in their package.json), which is between you and Bitwarden Inc. Read it
before installing or using them. Without them the server still starts;
the Secrets Manager tools then report that the SDK is not available.

Bitwarden Public API specification
----------------------------------
specs/public-api.spec.json in the repository is an empty placeholder
({"paths": {}}) and is not part of the npm package. `npm run
refresh-spec` replaces it with the Swagger document served by your own
Bitwarden instance; that document is Bitwarden's, is not covered by the
MIT License of this project, and should not be committed or published
from a fork without checking Bitwarden's terms. Tools generated from it
(`npm run generate`) derive their names and descriptions from it.

